  "query_preview": "..Monsoon moisture will return as early as tomorrow as \nhigh pressure reestablishes itself over Arizona. We have entered the \nshoulder season, so the moisture pool will occasionally retreat and \nthen move back northward as it interacts with troughs for the next \nseveral weeks. Eventually, these troughs will sweep the moisture out \npermanently, but this looks like it is at least 10 days out.\n\nSouthwest breezes will also pick up over the next few days as low \npressure passes to our north, but nothing that will need any \nheadlines.\n\nSo, this is the last very warm day, expect some cooling as showers \npick up heading into the weekend. We should dip back to normal \naround Monday or Tuesday.",
